PACK embed 1
IMPORT boot 1
IMPORT fetch 1
IMPORT semtext 1
IMPORT chat 1
IMPORT vector 1
RESIDENT Embed
-- SENTENCE VECTORS (#1143, stage 1 of the semantic field, docs/semtext-and-legs.md "Built: sentence vectors"): every sentence of a SemText gets an embedding vector, made by the local
-- Ollama through the Fetch driver, stored as the entity `Vector:of:<key>:s:<start>` ({of: the SemText's eid, start: the sentence's start in chars, v: the vector}), in a
-- GENTLE background queue. (The class `Vector` and its property `v` belong to the vector pack (packs/vector.c1f: a MAPPED class, f16, the first vector fixes the dimension); this pack only writes them.)
-- THE ASK: EVERY SemText is asked, with no flag (operator 2026-11-15): when a text gets its sentences (its text is written, by the chat on a message body and on an answer's body, by a Memory
-- note, by a model's pack on a leg of its own; a tool's result is not a SemText) and it is not yet `embedded`, `Embed:ask:<key>` ({of, state: pending, at}) is made; the ask is retired when the
-- text has all its vectors. `<key>` is the text's eid with `::` written `/` (`SemText.skey`).
-- THE BACKLOG: the bodies of the chat that no ask ever named (the imported history, the messages from before this pack) are found in the store, OLDEST first (by the message id), 64 texts a page
-- (`EmbedQueue.page`: a `sql`, re-asked as the cursor `after` moves), and queued the same way once the model server answers. A text that has all its vectors is marked `embedded = true`
-- (the page skips it), and the sentences done so far are counted in `emb_n` on the text (a text is embedded from its first sentence on; a restart goes on where it stopped).
-- THE QUEUE is the entity `Embed:queue` (EmbedQueue): `state` (idle | working | paused | stuck), `reason` (why it is stuck, as text), `line` (the sentence the Settings row `import.embeddings` shows:
-- done and total texts), `cur` (the text in work), `inflight` (the last request sent; `landed` is the last one whose receipt was taken), `cache`, `pass_n`, `hold`. A model reads it like any entity: a stuck queue is visible, never silent.
-- ONE REQUEST AT A TIME, one text per request, at most 64 sentences (a request is `POST <seat_backend>/api/embed {model: <embed_model>, input: [<sentences>]}`, 120 s limit): one request in flight is
-- within the existing worker limit (`effect_workers`: the Fetch effect takes a slot of its own, no second limit is made here). A request is sent only while NO chat turn is running (a `ChatTurn` in
-- state `running`); a request in flight finishes, then the queue waits for the turn to end: it pauses between requests and resumes by itself, because `go` is a getter that reads the turns.
-- A PASS is 256 sentences: the same-pass cache (`cache`, at most 64 [text, vector eid] pairs) lets a sentence said twice make no second request; it is emptied when the pass ends, and the next pass follows at once.
-- WHEN IT FAILS (the model server is not running, the model is not installed, a timeout, a wrong answer): `fail` says why (the reason is in `reason`, `line` and `state`), the pending sentences stay pending, and
-- the queue is held (`hold`) until the next change that is not its own: a chat event (a message, a turn starting or ending) or a new ask. Then, with no turn running, it tries again. No timer, no loop.
-- THE FACTS: `seat_backend` (the model server's address, launcher.c1f) and `embed_model` (the embedding model, launcher.c1f: mxbai-embed-large unless the launch says another).
-- THE RECEIPT of each request is the Fetch driver's receipt: an outside write, journalled, so a replay writes the same vectors without asking the model server. (`Fetch:embed` keeps the last receipt only:
-- its body is the vectors as text, a few hundred KB, replaced by the next request's.)

EmbedQueue.kind getter: 'queue'
EmbedAsk.kind getter: 'ask'

-- ---- the ask ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SemText.text on-setter embed-ask:
  WHEN this.text != None and strip(str(this.text)) != '' and this.embedded != True:
    membrane::Embed:ask[this.skey] = EmbedAsk(of: this.eid, state: 'pending', at: clock)
    membrane::Embed:queue.asked = (${'membrane::Embed:queue'}['asked'] or 0) + 1
-- a text that BECOMES a SemText after its text was written (a `Memory` note: its class list is written in answer to the text) is heard when its SemText getters arrive
SemText.skey on-setter embed-ask-late:
  WHEN this.text != None and strip(str(this.text)) != '' and this.embedded != True:
    membrane::Embed:ask[this.skey] = EmbedAsk(of: this.eid, state: 'pending', at: clock)
    membrane::Embed:queue.asked = (${'membrane::Embed:queue'}['asked'] or 0) + 1

-- ---- what a text still needs: its sentences from the `emb_n`-th on, at most 64 (the batch) ------------------------------------------------------------
SemText.emb_rest getter: tail(this.sentences, max(0, len(this.sentences) - (this.emb_n or 0)))
SemText.vec_todo getter: [{'eid': this.eid, 'skey': this.skey, 'start': s['start'], 'text': s['text'], 'veid': 'Vector:of:' + this.skey + ':s:' + str(s['start']), 'o': len([y for y in head(this.emb_rest, 64) if y['start'] < s['start']])} for s in head(this.emb_rest, 64)]

-- ---- start: the queue is born. A request the last run left out never gets its receipt: `run` (this run's start) is part of what says a request is in flight and of what a hold waits to see change,
-- so a new run is neither waiting for the dead request nor held by the dead run's failure. (Nothing else is written at start: a send can follow in the same cascade.)
Boot.started on-setter embed-seed:
  ALWAYS:
    membrane::Embed:queue = EmbedQueue(name: 'sentence vectors')

-- ---- the facts and the turns -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EmbedQueue.backend getter: ([b.seat_backend for b in instances('Boot') if b.seat_backend != None] or [None])[0]
EmbedQueue.model getter: ([b.embed_model for b in instances('Boot') if b.embed_model != None] or [None])[0]
-- A CHAT TURN IS RUNNING while an `Embed:turn:<key>` exists for this run. The turns are a lazy class (`instances('Chat')` would list only the loaded ones, and Chat cannot be resident), so each turn tells
-- us itself: the setter below makes a small entity of OUR resident class when any turn (the main chat's or a session's) becomes `running`, and retires it when the turn is done or an error (an abort and a refusal
-- end a turn the same way; `Boot.interrupted` ends the turns the last run left). `run` is the start of this run: an entity a dead run left is never counted.
EmbedTurn.kind getter: 'turn'
ChatTurn.state on-setter embed-turn:
  ALWAYS:
    FOR a IN ([1] if this.state == 'running' else []):
      ('membrane::Embed:turn:' + replace(this.eid, '::', '/')) = EmbedTurn(of: this.eid, run: ${'membrane::Embed:queue'}['run'])
    FOR a IN ([1] if this.state != 'running' and ${'membrane::Embed:turn:' + replace(this.eid, '::', '/')}['of'] != None else []):
      ('membrane::Embed:turn:' + replace(this.eid, '::', '/')).retire = True
EmbedQueue.busy getter: len([t for t in instances('Embed') if t.kind == 'turn' and t.run == this.run]) > 0
-- what a held queue waits to see change: the last chat event, and how many asks are pending
EmbedQueue.run getter: ([b.started for b in instances('Boot') if b.started != None] or [0])[0]
EmbedQueue.sig getter: str(this.run) + '/' + str(${'Doorbell:chat'}['at']) + '/' + str(len(this.asks))

-- ---- the work: asks first (oldest first), then the backlog page (oldest first): the vectors land in text order, so the field (packs/field.c1f) moves its entities in that order ----
EmbedQueue.asks getter: [${a}['of'] for a in sort_by([{'of': x.of, 'at': x.at or 0} for x in instances('Embed') if x.kind == 'ask' and x.state == 'pending'], 'at')]
EmbedQueue.page_rows getter: sql("SELECT k, sk, row_number() OVER (ORDER BY sk) AS n FROM (SELECT k, substr(k, instr(k, ':message:') + 9) AS sk FROM c_field WHERE cls = 'Chat' AND k LIKE '%:body' AND instr(k, ':message:') > 0 AND json_extract(body, '$.props.text') IS NOT NULL AND json_extract(body, '$.props.embedded') IS NULL) WHERE sk > ?1 AND (?2 = ?2 OR ?2 IS NULL) AND (?3 = ?3 OR ?3 IS NULL) ORDER BY sk LIMIT 64", this.after or '', ${'membrane::Legacy:seat'}['tick'], ${'Doorbell:chat'}['at'])
-- (no model or no server address: the backlog is not looked at, so reading it loads no stored text)
EmbedQueue.page getter: this.page_rows if this.page_rows is List and this.model != None and this.backend != None else []
EmbedQueue.texts getter: distinct(concat(head(this.asks, 64), [${r}['k'] for r in this.page]))
-- a stored text that is not loaded yet reads `vec_todo` as none: that is `not known`, never `nothing to do` (the first text not known yet makes the queue wait for it, so the order holds)
-- (a text whose own recall call is out, packs/mentions.c1f `in_flight`, waits: that call may make its vectors, `embed-ask-vectors` below; so does the body of a message queued for its turn,
-- whose recall call is about to be made (the banner asks it); once the turn starts or ends it is the queue's again)
EmbedQueue.open getter: [t for t in this.texts if ${t}['in_flight'] != True and not (tail(t, 5) == ':body' and ${head(t, len(t) - 5)}['queued'] == True and ${head(t, len(t) - 5)}['tstate'] == 'queued') and (not (${t}['vec_todo'] is List) or len(${t}['vec_todo']) > 0)]
EmbedQueue.cur getter: this.open[0] if len(this.open) > 0 and ${this.open[0]}['vec_todo'] is List else None
EmbedQueue.todo getter: ${this.cur}['vec_todo'] if this.cur != None else []

-- ---- a text with nothing left to embed is settled: marked, its ask retired, the cursor moves past the done front of the page --------------------------------
EmbedQueue.settled getter: [t for t in this.texts if ${t}['vec_todo'] is List and len(${t}['vec_todo']) == 0 and ${t}['embedded'] != True]
EmbedQueue.first_open getter: min([r['n'] for r in this.page if not (${r['k']}['vec_todo'] is List) or len(${r['k']}['vec_todo']) > 0] or [len(this.page) + 1])
-- the cursor moves only when the whole page is done (one query a page, not one a text: a `sql` holds the engine while it runs)
EmbedQueue.cut getter: this.page[-1]['sk'] if len(this.page) > 0 and this.first_open > len(this.page) else None
EmbedQueue.settled on-setter embed-settle:
  WHEN len(this.settled) > 0:
    FOR t IN this.settled:
      (t).embedded = True
      FOR a IN ([1] if ${'membrane::Embed:ask:' + ${t}['skey']}['of'] != None else []):
        ('membrane::Embed:ask:' + ${t}['skey']).retire = True
    this.made = (this.made or 0) + len(this.settled)
    FOR c IN ([this.cut] if this.cut != None else []):
      this.after = c

-- ---- the numbers: done and total texts (read from the store, asked again as a text is settled) ---------------------------------------------------------
EmbedQueue.counts_rows getter: sql("SELECT coalesce(sum(CASE WHEN json_extract(body, '$.props.embedded') IS NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END), 0) AS nleft, coalesce(sum(CASE WHEN json_extract(body, '$.props.embedded') IS NULL THEN 0 ELSE 1 END), 0) AS ndone FROM c_field WHERE cls = 'Chat' AND k LIKE '%:body' AND instr(k, ':message:') > 0 AND json_extract(body, '$.props.text') IS NOT NULL AND ?1 = ?1", 0)
EmbedQueue.counts getter: this.counts_rows[0] if this.counts_rows is List and len(this.counts_rows) > 0 else {}
-- THE NUMBERS are counted in memory from one start snapshot (the store's own count at the start: a count asked of the store after each text would lag by the cascade that wrote the last mark, and the store is
-- held while it is asked): done = the texts that had their vectors at the start + the texts this run settled; total = what the start found + the texts asked since. While a history import runs the total is
-- approximate: it never shows less than done plus the texts known to be waiting (the next start counts exactly).
EmbedQueue.done_n getter: (${this.counts}['ndone'] or 0) + (this.made or 0)
EmbedQueue.total_n getter: max((${this.counts}['ndone'] or 0) + (${this.counts}['nleft'] or 0) + (this.asked or 0), this.done_n + len(this.open))
EmbedQueue.progress getter: str(this.done_n) + ' of ' + str(this.total_n) + ' texts have sentence vectors'

-- ---- the state, as a word and as a sentence --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EmbedQueue.reason getter:
  WHEN this.fail != None: this.fail
  ELSE WHEN this.model == None: 'no embedding model is named (the embed_model fact)'
  ELSE WHEN this.backend == None: 'no model server address is known (the seat_backend fact)'
  ELSE: None
EmbedQueue.state getter:
  WHEN len(this.open) == 0 and not this.flying: 'idle'
  ELSE WHEN this.reason != None: 'stuck'
  ELSE WHEN this.flying: 'working'
  ELSE WHEN this.busy: 'paused'
  ELSE: 'working'
EmbedQueue.line getter:
  WHEN this.state == 'stuck': 'Sentence vectors are waiting: ' + str(this.reason) + ' (' + this.progress + '). The sentences stay pending; the queue tries again at the next quiet moment, when no chat turn is running.'
  ELSE WHEN this.state == 'paused': this.progress + '; paused while a chat turn runs'
  ELSE WHEN this.state == 'working': this.progress + '; the rest are being made in the background'
  ELSE: this.progress

-- ---- send: one request, only while no turn runs, none in flight, and not held ------------------------------------------------------------------------
EmbedQueue.ctexts getter: [c[0] for c in (this.cache or [])]
EmbedQueue.unc getter: [x for x in this.todo if not (x['text'] in this.ctexts)]
EmbedQueue.job getter:
  WHEN len(this.todo) == 0: None
  ELSE: {'eid': this.cur, 'upto': (${this.cur}['emb_n'] or 0) + len(this.todo), 'url': str(this.backend) + '/api/embed', 'model': this.model, 'n': len(this.todo), 'hit': [{'eid': x['eid'], 'start': x['start'], 'veid': x['veid'], 'src': [c[1] for c in this.cache if c[0] == x['text']][0]} for x in this.todo if x['text'] in this.ctexts], 'unc': [{'eid': x['eid'], 'start': x['start'], 'veid': x['veid'], 'text': x['text'], 'r': len([y for y in this.unc if y['o'] < x['o']])} for x in this.unc]}
-- a request is in flight from the send until its receipt is taken: the queue never clears `inflight` (a property is written once in a cascade, and the receipt's cascade goes on to the next send); `landed` names the last request whose receipt was taken
EmbedQueue.flying getter: this.inflight != None and ${this.inflight}['run'] == this.run and this.landed != ${this.inflight}['id']
EmbedQueue.ready getter: not this.flying and not this.busy and this.backend != None and this.model != None and this.hold != this.sig
EmbedQueue.go getter: this.job if this.ready and this.job != None else None
EmbedQueue.go on-setter embed-send:
  WHEN this.go != None:
    FOR h IN this.go['hit']:
      (h['veid']) = Vector(of: h['eid'], start: h['start'], v: ${h['src']}['v'])
    FOR c IN ([1] if len(this.go['unc']) == 0 else []):
      (this.go['eid']).emb_n = this.go['upto']
    FOR c IN ([1] if len(this.go['unc']) > 0 else []):
      ('Fetch:embed').request = {'id': 'embed:' + str((this.seq or 0) + 1), 'url': this.go['url'], 'method': 'POST', 'headers': {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}, 'body': {'model': this.go['model'], 'input': [x['text'] for x in this.go['unc']]}, 'timeout_s': 120}
      this.inflight = {'id': 'embed:' + str((this.seq or 0) + 1), 'run': this.run, 'eid': this.go['eid'], 'upto': this.go['upto'], 'url': this.go['url'], 'model': this.go['model'], 'n': this.go['n'], 'hit': this.go['hit'], 'unc': this.go['unc']}
      this.seq = (this.seq or 0) + 1

-- ---- the receipt -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Fetch.em_job getter: ${'membrane::Embed:queue'}['inflight']
Fetch.em_mine getter: startswith(str(${this.request_result}['id'] or ''), 'embed:') and ${this.em_job}['id'] == ${this.request_result}['id']
Fetch.em_body getter: json(str(${this.request_result}['body'] or '')) if this.em_mine else None
Fetch.em_vecs getter: (None if this.em_body is Error else ${this.em_body}['embeddings']) if this.em_mine else None
Fetch.em_why getter:
  WHEN not this.em_mine: None
  ELSE WHEN ${this.request_result}['status'] != 'ok': 'the model server did not answer at ' + str(${this.em_job}['url']) + ' (' + str(${this.request_result}['head']) + '). Is it running?'
  ELSE WHEN ${this.request_result}['http_status'] != 200: 'the model server answered ' + str(${this.request_result}['http_status']) + ' for the model ' + str(${this.em_job}['model']) + ': ' + str((None if this.em_body is Error else ${this.em_body}['error']) or ${this.request_result}['head']) + ' (a model that is not installed is installed with: ollama pull ' + str(${this.em_job}['model']) + ')'
  ELSE WHEN not (this.em_vecs is List) or len(this.em_vecs) != len(${this.em_job}['unc']) or len([v for v in this.em_vecs if not (v is List) or len(v) == 0]) > 0: 'the model server gave a wrong answer: expected ' + str(len(${this.em_job}['unc'])) + ' vectors in embeddings'
  ELSE: None
Fetch.em_ok getter: ${this.request_result}['id'] if this.em_mine and this.em_why == None else None

Fetch.em_why on-setter embed-failed:
  WHEN this.em_why != None:
    membrane::Embed:queue.fail = this.em_why
    membrane::Embed:queue.hold = ${'membrane::Embed:queue'}['sig']
    membrane::Embed:queue.landed = ${this.em_job}['id']

Fetch.em_ok on-setter embed-landed:
  WHEN this.em_ok != None:
    FOR it IN this.em_job['unc']:
      (it['veid']) = Vector(of: it['eid'], start: it['start'], v: this.em_vecs[it['r']])
    (this.em_job['eid']).emb_n = this.em_job['upto']
    FOR q IN ['membrane::Embed:queue']:
      (q).cache = [] if (${q}['pass_n'] or 0) + this.em_job['n'] >= 256 else tail(concat(${q}['cache'] or [], [[x['text'], x['veid']] for x in this.em_job['unc']]), 64)
      (q).pass_n = 0 if (${q}['pass_n'] or 0) + this.em_job['n'] >= 256 else (${q}['pass_n'] or 0) + this.em_job['n']
      (q).landed = ${this.em_job}['id']
      (q).fail = None

-- ---- a recall ask's own call that embedded the text's SENTENCES (packs/mentions.c1f `ask_input` a list: a Memory note) is this pipeline's request for them -----------------------
-- (operator 2026-11-15): its vectors are written as the sentence vectors and `emb_n` counts them, so the queue settles the text (`embedded`, its ask retired) and never sends it again.
SemText.ask_vecs on-setter embed-ask-vectors:
  WHEN this.ask_vecs != None and ${${this.ask_rr}['id']}['starts'] != None:
    sts = ${${this.ask_rr}['id']}['starts']
    FOR it IN [{'start': st, 'v': this.ask_vecs[len([y for y in sts if y < st])]} for st in sts]:
      ('Vector:of:' + this.skey + ':s:' + str(it['start'])) = Vector(of: this.eid, start: it['start'], v: it['v'])
    this.emb_n = max(this.emb_n or 0, len(sts))
